FastAPI Installation, Project Structure & Your First REST API
Week 2 · Backend Engineering
Today we move from understanding APIs to actually building them using FastAPI and Python.
By the end of this lesson, you will have a working backend application running locally in VS Code, with interactive Swagger documentation.
This is the foundation for the AI Platform Gateway project you'll build during this preparation.
1. What is FastAPI?
FastAPI is a modern Python framework used to build APIs.
It provides:
•	Fast HTTP API development.
•	Automatic request validation.
•	Automatic API documentation.
•	Python type-hint support.
•	Asynchronous endpoint support.
•	Integration with AI models and databases.
3.1. Introduction to FastAPI: Lightweight Python Framework to Build APIs | by Kumar Harsh | Medium
Where does FastAPI fit in an AI platform?
Frontend Application
       |
       | HTTP Request
       v
   FastAPI Backend
       |
       v
  Business Logic
       |
       +------ Model Manager
       |
       +------ Database
       |
       +------ LLM Provider
       |
       v
  JSON Response
       |
       v
Frontend Application
For example, when a user submits a question to your AI platform, FastAPI receives the request and coordinates the required processing.
2. Install FastAPI in VS Code
We'll use your Windows and VS Code environment.
Step 1 — Create a project folder
Create a folder manually:
E:\AIDSML\ChtGpt\Day-09\Projects\AIPlatformGateway
Open this folder in VS Code.
Step 2 — Open the terminal
In VS Code:
1.	Click Terminal.
2.	Select New Terminal.
3.	Check that the terminal is PowerShell.
4.	Confirm that the terminal is inside your project directory.
Step 3 — Create a virtual environment
Run:
python -m venv .venv
This creates an isolated Python environment for the project.
Activate it:
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
If PowerShell blocks activation because of the execution policy, run this command in the current terminal:
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
Then activate again:
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
You should see:
(.venv) PS D:\Gaurev\Projects\AIPlatformGateway>
Step 4 — Install dependencies
Run: 
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
Then:
pip install "fastapi[standard]"
This installs FastAPI and its standard development dependencies, including the server tooling.
Verify:
pip show fastapi
It will show:
Name: fastapi
Version: 0.165.0
Summary: FastAPI framework, high performance, easy to learn, fast to code, ready for production
Home-page: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi
